are no hundreds, tens, ones, tenths and hundredths in the given expression, which means that we have $0$ hundreds, $0$ tens, $0$ ones, $0$ tenths, and $0$ hundredths.\nPutting this into the place value chart, we get:\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>thousands</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>hundreds</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>tens</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>ones</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>tenths</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>hundredths</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\"><strong>thousandths</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>.</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nTherefore, the given expanded form is equivalent to $5,000.001$."] [:db/cas 17592186138248 :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the place value chart for $12.5$:\n\n| **tens** | **ones** |  | **tenths** | **hundredths** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $1$ | $2$ | **.** | $5$ |  |\n\nThen, we move all digits by one place to the *right.*\n\n| **tens** | **ones** |  | **tenths** | **hundredths** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n|  | $\\bbox[3pt, lightgray]{1}$ | **.** | $2$ | $\\bbox[3pt, lightgray]{5}$ |\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n12.5\\div 1